{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1020399-nephandi-and-rotes","id":1020399,"title":"Nephandi and Rotes?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-12-21T07:54:26-08:00","id":1020399,"title":"Nephandi and Rotes?","content":"so, im reading The Book of Madness and it keeps mentioning how the Nephandi are &quot;Subtle.&quot;. Its hard to imagine coming from the &quot;Hail Satan -Lets eat babies- Army&quot; but.. is there any examples of how subtle they are? or how do they actually fight ? i read here and there that some of them can shoot bolts of lightning but i dont think they use this all the time (because, well..paradox is a biatch).<br /> So yeah, im curious to know how do they exactly use their magick and how do the Barrabi pull punches while in a fight","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-21T09:43:05-08:00","id":1020448,"title":"","content":"I think the biggest thing here is that a Nephandi that gets called out in a fight has already failed in their most common goal... And that is corruption. The subtle part is that, in game, you never know who might be a Nephandi. Their best effects are to conceal who they really are and what they are really doing. Aura sight would get fooled by an aura alteration effect. Scrying would hit interference or even a false result (past sight to see who murdered important NPC X gets a result of Ally Y instead of Villian Z, etc). Ring of Truth would get muffled by the Silence of Lies, etc, etc.<br /> <br /> If/When a Nephandi does get into a fight (and the fight isn't a distraction for something else), they wouldn't pull any punches. If they learned any weaknesses of the PCs (phobias, self-control issues, etc.) they would use them without remorse. If the characters don't come away from a Nephandi fight without loosing something important (an ally, trust issues, utter break of confidence, etc), that Fallen didn't belong in the Cauls anyway.<br /> <br /> As for what effects, specifically? Well, each has their own style, but Entropy and Mind come in real handy with hiding true intentions, so it makes sense that curses and psychic warfare would also be on the table. Correspondence and/or Spirit for a fast getaway also means allies/minions are only a vile curse away. Look for how a Nephandi goes about their day to day business, see what Spheres are needed for that first and then work offense / defense from there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12655-tzizimine","name":"tzizimine","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-21T09:50:37-08:00","id":1020452,"title":"","content":"There are nephandi that will just go on killing sprees, showering the streets with lightning and fire calling out in the name of their dark lord. Those guys don't tend to last very long.<br /> Rather, the nephandi prefer to get others to carry out their work for them. Rather than take a gun to a school and have at it, they'd enrol as a teacher, teach a few classes and get a good idea on the social climate of the kids. Then he'll start to put in place subtle things to encourage bullying, isolation, or even encourage the use of divisive and dismissive rhetoric. They'll turn the school into a place which churns out close-minded selfish children, with a do or die mentality and a deep hate in their hearts. If anyone starts to catch on to this, then all they need do is target a specific student into isolation and slowly encourage them to hate the other kids so badly that they go on a shooting spree themselves. Any kids that could speak out against the teacher will get killed, and everyone else will be too stricken with grief to care. A lot of noise will be made about gun control but nothing will actually change.<br /> <br /> How the nephandi does this will depend on the specific circumstances.<br /> Entropy is one of their most favoured spheres, and they'd use this a lot to get an idea down for their plans, as well as to gently influence decay in various ways, enforcing a feeling of negativity amongst the students.<br /> Mind can be very useful to implanting ideas, suggestions, and thoughts, while Life can be great for causing all manner of embarrassment to the kids, or making certain faculty members require a quick substitute.<br /> <br /> The way they conduct their magic depends very much on their paradigm, but even the more outlandish focuses can be gotten away with. I'm sure we've heard of a fair few teachers that was rumoured to have monkey's paw, a skull, or a human eyeball in their desk. Perhaps they can use the intestines they cut in disections during biology class, or simply by focusing on the misery they bring to the children they teach.<br /> <br /> If done right, no one will think of the nephandi as anything more than a disgruntled teacher, heck they might even think of them as a model educator who could very well be in the running for Head of Department, or even the Principle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}